,[7139420,20403,3,0.121,0.072,[[14,14]],[],0,323],[7139982,20404,28,0.796,0.587,[[5,0.7,49,20],[15,0.3,29,8]],[],0,324],[7140018,20404,61,1.144,0.818,[[5,0.603,50,37],[15,0.397,30,24]],[],0,325],[7213203,20424,2,0.09,0.052,[[5,51]],[],0,326],[7228414,20427,47,1.326,1.047,[[7,0.717,16,35],[17,0.226,2,10],[8,0.057,28,2]],[],0,327],[7229052,20431,40,1.326,1.047,[[18,8]],[["7ea974e9_2182b31f",26,-4,0,"I don't think this approach is ideal. All of Glic's is-enabled checks are concentrated in `GlicEnabling` and that's where the has-consented logic should be updated. The `HasConsentedForProfile` above…"]],0,328],[7232779,20431,98,2.344,1.853,[[18,0.865,9,87],[13,0.067,12,6],[14,0.048,15,4],[17,0.019,3,1]],[["51b6d66c_da5889aa",3,-1,0,"can you fix the CL description?"],["efb663a8_5f4a2320",27,-1,1,"I kind of feel these comments could be slightly more verbose and explain what these values actually do. But I don't have much context here, so..."],["01e047df_aa0efd04",28,0,1,"nit/optional: could add a CHECK that both arms are not simultaneously enabled."],["f25cae10_d3d26f35",3,0,1,"nit: Prefer b:123 for internal issues ```suggestion Bug: b:466003561 ```"]],0,329],[7239512,20432,93,2.344,1.853,[[18,10]],[],0,330],[7248157,20439,330,7.579,6.176,[[18,0.53,11,177],[19,0.223,0,75],[13,0.16,13,51],[14,0.074,16,25],[8,0.011,29,2]],[["0e8135b4_54ce6320",28,-2,1,"let's configure https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:chrome/browser/glic/test_support/glic_test_environment.h;l=70 for this test fixture instead of undoing the initial FRE state…"],["1a54e737_febf764d",28,-2,1,"let's move this back to where it was"],["51159588_2c746842",26,-2,1,"should we still report this action? How about other actions in this file? It might be nice to have a glic_fre.h/cc file to store FRE related code, instead of moving…"],["6a49dfb4_5896b25d",29,-2,1,"normally, we would expose an ObservableValue<boolean> which is signaled when the value changes. I think we will want to do that here too, to allow coordination w/ mulitple glic instances."],["89d9fa33_759ebadf",30,-2,1,"these functions should be set to undefined when kGlicTrustFirstOnboarding is not enabled. See the constructor of this class for similar examples"],["b380b8ce_65ee0f83",31,-2,1,"add a ForTesting suffix"],["c3bd1909_ca6f40ed",29,-2,0,"Should the web client assume the FRE is completed if these functions do not exist?"],["19912cd4_59aeba79",30,-1,1,"instead of sending a message, just send the initial value in the initial state"],["8421a45c_98fcdc0c",27,-1,1,"normally, we would send the initial state over in WebClientInitialState, then you don't need a function to query the state."],["90d9beb1_9bbabca3",32,-1,1,"don't need this anymore"],["e493a93f_44ba44a6",30,-1,1,"nit: no need to do this conditionally, you're already setting onboardingCompleted unconditionally elsewhere anyway"],["fae4cb4a_6877fc80",33,-1,1,"this isn't needed anymore"]],0,331]]}